{"resourceIdentifier":"5085","resourceName":"Tond Tenga","description":"Tree Aid (TA) is an international development non-governmental organisation (INGO) that focuses on working with people in the Sahel region of Africa to tackle poverty and the effects of climate change by growing trees, improving people's incomes, and restoring and protecting land. It is a registered charity in the UK. TA is partnering with Earthshot Labs PBC (Earthshot) and Capricorn Investment Group LLC (Capricorn) to restore degraded landscapes in Burkina Faso through enrichment planting and agroforestry activities.\r\nTA has partnered with local communities to identify 37 sites of degraded woodland and shrublands located in 18 communes and 4 regions with the potential to become new forest sites through enrichment planting. These sites have been affected by deforestation and decades of unsustainable agricultural activity, leading to soil degradation that has prevented further agricultural activity. This has resulted in desertification and the loss of access to culturally relevant non-timber forest products (NTFPs) that are extremely significant in socio-economic terms. Thus, the project identified activities in enrichment planting and agroforestry to restore native forests and increase access to NFTPs. \r\nThrough enrichment planting, the project will restore native tree species with high importance to the biodiversity of the area, high restoration potential and some NTFP uses. In total 12,000 ha will be targeted across these 37 forest sites. In total just over 142,500 trees will be targeted on farmland in and around the 37 forest sites.\r\nThe project is estimated to remove 3.7 million tCO2e during the project lifetime, with estimated annual GHG emission removals of 92,576.9 tCO2e.","location":{"latitude":11.970340,"longitude":-0.728066},"inPublicCommentPeriod":false,"lastPublicCommentPeriod":{"startInclusive":"2024-05-23","endExclusive":"2024-06-23","endInclusive":"2024-06-22"},"attributes":